  "refMeasuredMood": "Your daily self-rating from 1 to 10 in the Captain's log, compared with your own baseline.",
  "refWhyMood": "Small, steady dips in mood are easier to fix early. Watching mood against your baseline is more useful than any single day.",
  "refTodoMood": "Log honestly, then pick one small action. Tell a crewmate if low days keep adding up.",
  "refMeasuredStress": "Your daily stress rating from 1 to 10, compared with your own baseline. Higher is less favourable.",
  "refWhyStress": "Long confinement keeps stress levels raised. Rising stress also tends to cut into sleep and focus.",
  "refTodoStress": "Slow your breathing for two minutes, move your body, or hand off one task for today.",
  "refMeasuredSleep": "Hours slept each night, from the sleep tracker or sample data. 7 to 8 hours is the healthy range; 6 hours or less is short sleep.",
  "refWhySleep": "Sleep loss and irregular schedules slow reactions, lower mood and make small problems feel bigger.",
  "refTodoSleep": "Keep a fixed lights-out time, dim screens an hour before and cool the cabin for a sleep reset.",
  "refMeasuredFocus": "Your focus rating from 1 to 10, together with the lapse count from the reaction test.",
  "refWhyFocus": "Attention is the first thing to slip when sleep or workload goes wrong, and errors cost the most in flight.",
  "refTodoFocus": "Take a real break away from screens, then do one task at a time. Check your sleep first.",
  "refMeasuredMotivation": "Your engagement rating from 1 to 10, compared with your own baseline.",
  "refWhyMotivation": "Long, repetitive missions invite boredom. Falling engagement can come before low mood.",
  "refTodoMotivation": "Start a small new project or change the order of your day for variety.",
  "refMeasuredConnection": "Your crew connection rating from 1 to 10, compared with your own baseline.",
  "refWhyConnection": "Good teamwork depends on feeling connected. Distance from Earth also makes contact with family slower and rarer.",
  "refTodoConnection": "Share a meal with the crew or send a message home. Small contact counts.",
  "refMeasuredWorkload": "Your workload rating from 1 to 10, compared with your own baseline. Higher is less favourable.",
  "refWhyWorkload": "Work overload eats into sleep. With delays to Earth, crews must manage their own pace.",
  "refTodoWorkload": "Move one task to tomorrow, or ask the crew to share it. Protect your sleep window.",
  "refMeasuredReaction": "A 3-minute reaction test. You tap as fast as you can when a stimulus appears. We record your mean response time, lapses (slower than 500 ms) and false starts.",
  "refWhyReaction": "Slow or lapsing responses are one of the earliest signs of fatigue and drifting attention, often before you feel it yourself.",
  "refTodoReaction": "Repeat the test every few days at a similar time of day, and compare with your own baseline.",
